{'job_id': '4314348459', 'job_title': 'Physiotherapist', 'company_name': 'TBI Health Group New Zealand', 'company_logo': 'https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/C4D0BAQEW5H-Fb2WQcQ/company-logo_100_100/company-logo_100_100/0/1631311318151?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=A5JR7i_ZPzVhEltRuQfc6lUlWtwuhpeoIPZ_EQItxYQ', 'location': 'Paraparaumu, Wellington, New Zealand', 'posted_date': '3 weeks ago', 'num_applicants': None, 'job_description': 'Introduction:About TBI HealthTBI Health was created with a simple idea: to help people with pain, illness, or injury. TBI Health has come a long way since it began its journey in 2001, from 2016 we partnered with Southern Cross & together we are passionate about ensuring our clients get the right help, at the right time, to get them back on track & living meaningful lives.We are known to offer an attractive work environment to support staff wellbeing and growth. Our current focus is to continue our work on introducing new services for our staff to become involved in and ultimately, help enhance their careers.It is also important to TBI Health to continue having an equity focused workplace culture where staff feel supported, enriched, & valued. As a NZ owned company, we position ourselves as a Te Tiriti partner and have an ongoing commitment to health equity for Māori. Join us on this transformational journey of delivering tailored and quality healthcare service which meets the needs of our diverse Aotearoa.Description:About The Mahi (Role)We are on the lookout for a motivated and experienced Physiotherapist to join our expanding Kapiti team in Wellington!This is afull-time, permanent role(Monday to Friday, 40 hours per week), working 100% in ourbrand new, spacious clinic, complete with your own air-conditioned treatment room, in-clinic gym, and access to SNAP Fitness next door.You will join acollaborative and supportive multidisciplinary team, and we are especially looking for someone excited to grow their expertise in theIntegrated Care Pathways (ICP) contract.Full training and mentoring will be provided.In this role, you will:Provide high-quality, evidence-based physiotherapyAssess and treat clients with a variety of MSK conditionsCollaborate with funders, employers, and your MDT colleaguesMaintain accurate clinical documentation and case notesContribute to team meetings and weekly CPD/in-service sessionsGain experience across a range of ACC contracts, including ICP, Pain, Med Fees, and Training for IndependenceIf you are keen to learn and passionate about helping clients achieve great outcomes, this is an excellent opportunity to grow your physiotherapy career.About The Kapiti TeamOur Kapiti team is a vibrant, multicultural group that values connection, collaboration, and delivering high-quality care. You will bebased at our modern, purpose-built clinicat 144 Kapiti Road, just a short walk from local shops and cafes.You will work alongside an experienced hand therapist, a women’s health physio, a pain management physio, hospital and community physiotherapists, and two friendly admins. We have a close-knit, supportive culture, complete with regular team lunches and opportunities for professional collaboration.We are deeplycommitted to equityand continually growing our cultural capability. Building strong, respectful relationships with Māori health providers and local iwi is central to how we deliver care that truly reflects and supports the diverse needs of our region.Skills and Experiences:About YouThis is a clinical role, so you will need aBachelor’s degree in Physiotherapy, along with a current practising certificate and indemnity insurance to work in Aotearoa, New Zealand.We welcome physiotherapists with2-5 years’ clinical experiencewho are passionate about delivering high-quality care.Previous experience with ACC contracts is an advantage but not essential, as comprehensive orientation and ongoing training will be provided, including ICP contract management and key worker tasks.To be successful in this role, you will have:Strong clinical reasoning and confident decision-makingClear, concise report writingCommitment to clinical excellence and continuous learningA professional, positive, and proactive attitudeExcellent time management and communication skillsAbility to work independently while contributing to a teamStrong client focus and understanding of quality service deliveryAwareness of what good customer service looks like in healthcareWillingness to learn and develop skills in ACC contract managementBenefits Of Joining TBI HealthWe value your contribution and are committed to supporting your well-being, growth, and career development. At TBI Health, you will enjoy:Competitive salary plus performance bonusesSubsidised Southern Cross health insuranceWellness allowance and birthday leaveEmployee Assistance Programme (EAP) supportReimbursement for APC, professional membership, and indemnity insuranceExtensive internal training, orientation, and ongoing mentoringAnnual CPD contribution and access to regular MDT meetings, in-services, and case reviewsMāori tikanga training sessions throughout the yearClear career pathways into leadership, research, quality, and senior clinician rolesConveniently located on the sunny Kapiti Coast — close to shops, motorway on-ramp, and easy parkingHear From Our TeamFrom Karen, Physiotherapist:“I’ve only been at TBI for a short time but so far have been really impressed with how welcoming everyone is. I love working in a small, local clinic, but it’s reassuring to have the resources and experience of a nationwide company behind you. The support from TBI is great and there’s plenty of opportunities for further training. My small team is lovely and friendly, and they’ve helped me to feel settled really quickly. I’m looking forward to expanding my skills as a therapist in some new areas with TBI behind me.”Click here to read more staff testimonials or find out about us: https://tbihealth.co.nz/careers/staff-testimonials/How To ApplyExcited about this role? Don’t wait, get in touch with us NOW to explore your future with TBI Health!Applications close on 17th November 2025We will be reviewing and interviewing candidates as they apply. That means we may fill the position sooner, so if this sounds like the opportunity you have been waiting for, reach out ASAP!Please include a cover letter with your application. All correspondence will be kept strictly confidential.Have questions or want to learn more? Contact Clinic Manager Sean Dalton on 0273590066 or sean.dalton@tbihealth.co.nzWe welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds who meet the skills and qualifications for this role.Please note: All applications must be submitted via the online process. Applications sent directly by email will not be considered for shortlisting.', 'seniority_level': 'Mid-Senior level', 'employment_type': 'Full-time', 'job_function': 'Health Care Provider', 'industries': ['Wellness and Fitness Services'], 'job_url': 'https://nz.linkedin.com/jobs/view/physiotherapist-at-tbi-health-group-new-zealand-4314348459', 'company_url': 'https://nz.linkedin.com/company/tbi-health-group?trk=public_jobs_topcard-org-name', 'source': 'linkedin', 'scraped_at': '2025-11-14T18:51:37.450315'}